<p>A U.S. submarine sank the Iranian warship IRIS Dena in the Indian Ocean near Sri Lanka this week, killing Iranian sailors and pushing the U.S.-Iran conflict closer to the busy sea lanes off South Asia. Sri Lankan authorities then took custody of a second Iranian vessel, evacuating and assisting its crew after the ship sought help near Sri Lankan waters. Colombo said it acted on humanitarian grounds while staying neutral. The fallout has quickly become a diplomatic and legal test for Sri Lanka and nearby India. U.S. officials have urged Sri Lanka not to send Iranian sailors back to Iran, according to reporting that cites an internal U.S. memo or cable. Indian outlets also noted that the IRIS Dena recently took part in India’s MILAN 2026 naval exercise and related fleet events, adding political sensitivity in New Delhi as it tries to balance ties with Washington and Tehran.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/anCGsZN0Cyt836a9jLaEIg52SuSfS1oKW2R7fpPaUuB8jURjDO76ilfyxiYEsb0HsMSwhTU071z4hVXBnHH-fOQIq6uU2U4HLq__mWWPrTrv1cx5Mxv6ROQ-eVwCPKE5dEmeTMa5MDMiYiaKTeZbseY2pHqT8jOkGUUQViTjtwmHesaLAzggtojg8yVdPUV9YJD1_DyyEKh6Hz4F2w3qHcQ' alt='An injured Iranian sailor is moved on a stretcher at Galle National Hospital in Sri Lanka after the torpedoing of the Iranian naval ship IRIS Dena on Thursday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Survivors count: Reporting says 32 sailors survived the sinking of the IRIS Dena, and they are among those the U.S. urged Sri Lanka not to repatriate to Iran.</li><li>Australians aboard: Australia’s prime minister said three Australians were serving on the U.S. submarine involved in the attack, fueling debate at home about the risks of close operational cooperation with the United States.</li><li>Where it happened: The sinking happened about 19 nautical miles off Sri Lanka’s southern port city of Galle, alarming the region because it was so close to major Indian Ocean shipping routes.</li><li>India’s dilemma: Indian commentary noted the IRIS Dena had been an invited participant in India-hosted MILAN-linked events (including high-visibility fleet activities), complicating how New Delhi signals condolences, maritime posture, and crisis diplomacy after a ship recently treated as a guest was later sunk nearby.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Sri Lankan government: President Anura Kumara Dissanayake said Sri Lanka would safeguard neutrality in the wider conflict and not allow its territory to be used by any party, while still taking steps needed to protect human life as it evacuated the second ship’s crew. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/sri-lanka-says-second-iranian-ship-awaits-entry/article70706664.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>United States (diplomatic mission in Colombo): An internal U.S. cable/memo described U.S. diplomats urging Sri Lanka not to repatriate the IRIS Bushehr crew or survivors from the IRIS Dena to Iran. (<a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/us-presses-sri-lanka-not-to-repatriate-iris-booshehr-crew-32-iris-dena-survivors-to-iran-13987009.html'>Firstpost</a>)</li><li>Australian government: Prime Minister Anthony Albanese publicly confirmed that three Australians were serving on the U.S. submarine involved in sinking the IRIS Dena, prompting questions at home about the implications of deep military integration with the U.S. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/06/world/middleeast/iran-warship-us-submarine-australia.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Indian media analysis: Indian coverage argued that because the IRIS Dena had recently been India’s invitee at India-hosted naval events, New Delhi faces an added moral obligation over how it publicly responds—on top of the strategic pressure created by the crisis unfolding near key regional sea lanes. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/opinion/iran-israel-war-india-and-the-iran-row-that-should-never-have-been-11180856#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li><li>Al Jazeera explainer: Al Jazeera framed the sinking as a deliberate U.S. decision to target a high-profile Iranian vessel, asking what strategic purpose Washington sought by striking the IRIS Dena. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/3/6/why-did-the-us-torpedo-irans-prize-warship'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/opinion/iran-israel-war-india-and-the-iran-row-that-should-never-have-been-11180856#publisher=newsstand'>Opinion: Opinion | Iran And The Actual Questions India Should Be Asking About IRIS Dena Storm</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/videos/iranian-warship-strike-near-sri-lanka-raises-questions-for-india/article70713451.ece'>Watch: Iranian warship strike near Sri Lanka raises questions for India</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/03/06/g-s1-112759/after-the-u-s-sinks-an-iranian-warship-sri-lanka-takes-custody-of-an-iranian-vessel'>After the U.S. sinks an Iranian warship, Sri Lanka takes custody of an Iranian vessel</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c4geelnw7w3o'>The final voyage of the Iranian warship sunk by the US</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/06/world/middleeast/iran-warship-us-submarine-australia.html'>3 Australians Were on U.S. Submarine That Sank an Iranian Warship</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/3/6/why-did-the-us-torpedo-irans-prize-warship'>Why did the US torpedo Iran’s ‘prize’ warship?</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/us-presses-sri-lanka-not-to-repatriate-iris-booshehr-crew-32-iris-dena-survivors-to-iran-13987009.html'>US presses Sri Lanka not to repatriate IRIS Booshehr crew, 32 IRIS Dena survivors to Iran</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/634017-sri-lanka-takes-custody-iris-bushehr/'>Sri Lanka takes custody of second Iranian ship after rescuing crew</a> - rt.com</li></ul>